<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dionysiou Monastery</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1370s</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dionysiou Monastery is an Eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-orthodox-church">Orthodox</a> monastery on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mount-athos">Mount Athos</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>, built on a rock above the sea on the peninsula's south-west coast. It was founded in the 1370s by the monk Dionysios of Korisos with the support of Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexios-iii-of-trebizond">Alexios III of Trebizond</a>, whose chrysobull of 1374 survives in its archive. It ranks fifth among the twenty ruling monasteries of Athos.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dionysiou-monastery.jpg" alt="Dionysiou Monastery" width="320" height="224" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Explorer1940 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Athos_--_Dionysiou_Monastery_03.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
